  "notes": [
    "A beamforming report is a digital payload: every receiver that decodes the frame obtains the same angle bits. The receiver changes only WHICH reports are heard and how much of each body is kept (512-byte firmware cap in B). Receiver and months therefore change together, but the angle content can only differ by time, not by receiver.",
    "Bins kept = bins fully covered in every B window of the gallery (AND over devices); the same mask is applied to A, including in the A_within_A reference.",
    "Devices absent from B (AppleTV-BR, Vacuum; Laptop has 114 Nr=4 reports in July only, first column undecodable at Nr=4) cannot be queried; chance is 1/|gallery| of devices present in both sets.",
    "A device whose majority format differs between A and B (per_device.format_differs_*) can never be matched by the format one-hot across sets; its angle features are compared in radians (angles) and after re-quantisation to 4/2 bits (angles_rq)."
